```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
  // Allow the requested pitch at any radius, including the fully zoomed-out start radius.
  camera.limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;
  camera.pitch = pitch;
}
```

I disabled the radius-based pitch clamp on the camera’s limits and then set the requested pitch, leaving zoom, heading, and centre untouched. I’m relying on the notes since I can’t run the library, and I’m not sure whether your app later replaces `camera.limits`, which would re-enable the clamp.
